From: Project Cascadia <noreply@cascadia>
Subject: [PATCH] smp: start the secondary CPUs on T8030 (A13)

smp_start_secondaries() gave up on T8030 ("CPU start offset is unknown
for this SoC"), so Linux came up on one core of six.

- The PMGR CPU start registers sit at 0xd4000 as on A11 (+0x4 system
  start bits, +0x8 + 4 * cluster core start); the t8030 QEMU model that
  boots iOS treats a write to PMGR 0xd4004 as the CPU release. The ADT
  agrees on the masks: each cpu's function-enable_core points at the
  PMGR with 1 << (4 * cluster + core).
- A13 has no midr_parts[] entry, so it runs with features_unknown and
  the generic code never writes RVBAR. IORVBAR is MMIO and writable from
  EL1 when unlocked: point it at our vectors in that case, and print what
  was found, so a locked RVBAR shows up in the log.

diff --git a/src/smp.c b/src/smp.c
index 83eadff..f69e732 100644
--- a/src/smp.c
+++ b/src/smp.c
@@ -124,7 +124,19 @@ static void smp_start_cpu(int index, int die, int cluster, int core, u64 impl, u
     if (spin_table[index].flag)
         return;
 
-    if (!cpu_features->apple_sysregs_unlocked &&
+    if (chip_id == T8030) {
+        /*
+         * A13 runs with features_unknown (no A12/A13 entry in midr_parts[]),
+         * so the generic path below would leave RVBAR alone. IORVBAR is MMIO,
+         * writable from EL1 as long as iBoot did not lock it: point it at our
+         * vectors if it is unlocked, and say what we found either way.
+         */
+        u64 rvbar = read64(impl);
+        if (!(rvbar & RVBAR_LOCK))
+            write64(impl, (u64)_vectors_start);
+        printf("RVBAR @0x%lx: 0x%lx -> 0x%lx (vectors 0x%lx)\n", impl, rvbar, read64(impl),
+               (u64)_vectors_start);
+    } else if (!cpu_features->apple_sysregs_unlocked &&
         (read64(impl) & RVBAR_ADDR) != (u64)_vectors_start) {
         printf("Failed! \n    RVBAR (=0x%lx) is locked and differs from entry point (=0x%lx)\n",
                read64(impl) & RVBAR_ADDR, (u64)_vectors_start);
@@ -290,6 +302,7 @@ void smp_start_secondaries(void)
         case T8011:
         case T8012:
         case T8015:
+        case T8030: // A13: PMGR CPU start at 0xd4004/0xd4008 as on A11
             cpu_start_off = CPU_START_OFF_S8000;
             break;
         case T8103:
diff --git a/src/soc.h b/src/soc.h
index 31391f9..63ca5af 100644
--- a/src/soc.h
+++ b/src/soc.h
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
 #define T8011    0x8011
 #define T8012    0x8012
 #define T8015    0x8015
+#define T8030    0x8030
 
 #define T8103 0x8103
 #define T8112 0x8112
